+# Command Center SIP scanner
+
+Approved intent: prepare history before open, rank completed opening-window volume after 09:35 Eastern, authenticate the Command Center read, and test the paper entry/exit loop. The owner said “please proceed”; implementation stays native in this session. Platform main and native production branches are not modified by development.
+
+## Contract and strategy
+
+Dedicated version-1 snapshot: version=1, status=ready, session_date, generated_at, window_start, window_end, candidates (symbol, price, rvol, atr14, avg_vol), coverage and exclusions. Window is exactly 09:30–09:35 America/New_York. Filters are price > 5, 20 completed-session average daily share volume >= 1 million, Wilder ATR14 > 0.50; rank by descending opening-share-volume / mean of 14 prior opening-window share volumes, deterministic symbol tie-break, max 20. Eligibility history and opening baseline never include today's partial data. No new minimum RVOL threshold or change to trading signals, sizing, stops or paper mode.
+
+Universe is current ALL_SYMBOLS with verified non-fund sector classifications in SYMBOL_SECTOR; missing classification is excluded visibly. ETFs/funds are excluded, not hand-maintained or inferred from ticker spelling. The configured set is not claimed to be all US stocks.
+
+## Preparation and publication
+
+A read-only Schwab adapter uses existing platform token refresh, GET marketdata pricehistory/quotes only, bounded timeouts, one 401 refresh/retry; safe codes only, no response bodies/credentials. Preparation caches daily eligibility and complete 14-session opening-window totals in Redis per trading date. Two price-history reads per stock; one multi-session minute request replaces 14 separate historical requests. Rate-limited concurrency is 4. A preparation deadline retains successful per-symbol rows for retry, not a misleading complete result. Ineligible stocks need no opening-history request. Missing/incomplete history excludes that stock with a durable reason; transport/auth/storage failures prevent a ready snapshot and are retried in the scheduled window. New data never silently overwrites a ready result for the same session.
+
+Redis keys use cc:sip:v1 prefix, seven-day retention for diagnostics. Redis availability is required: no in-process fallback. Per-session work locks have unique owners and compare-and-delete release. Prepared rows are date/version scoped; results use an atomic SET NX so an existing ready result is immutable. Preparation progress is recorded per symbol so repeated invocations only retry unfinished failures. Counts/reasons are retained in preparation and result records and JSON logs; existing cron run logging is reused. No database migration.
+
+One new logical cron job chooses phase by ET time: preparation 09:00–09:30, publication 09:35–09:40. Logical expressions 0-25/5 13,14 * * 1-5 and 35-39 13,14 * * 1-5; New York and exchange-holiday guards accept the correct DST candidate. Job policy timeout 280000 ms, lock 330 s, no money-path effects. SIP_SCANNER_ENABLED is an explicit false-by-default deployment switch. Existing physical minute dispatcher stays unchanged.
+
+## Machine interface
+
+GET /api/internal/cc/sip-scanner serves only stored results for today's ET trading date. Separate SIP_SCANNER_SECRET, minimum 32 characters, must differ from CRON_SECRET, DASHBOARD_PASSWORD, MONITOR_SECRET and SCHWAB_BROKER_SECRET. Header-only Bearer authentication, private/no-store responses, no browser-user entitlement requirement and no provider calls during reads. Disabled route=404, bad auth=401, missing config/storage=503, result not yet ready=202 with Retry-After, ready=200. Cron guard accepts CRON_SECRET only. Read errors never look like a healthy empty list.
+
+## Command Center consumer
+
+SCANNER_SECRET in the SIP bot's gitignored local environment authenticates HTTPS requests; localhost HTTP is allowed for isolated tests only. No redirects or response/URL/credential text in errors. Strict version/date/window/age/row validation rejects stale, future, malformed and cross-day snapshots. Ready snapshots must be generated no earlier than window end and no older than five minutes on first selection. Explicit ready candidates=[] is valid. No fabricated RVOL or silent legacy-response acceptance.
+
+Transient HTTP 429/5xx, 202, transport failures and readiness races yield UniversePending. SessionRunner retries on its normal polls until 09:40 without entries; existing position management runs first. At the deadline, mark the scanner unavailable, stop further entry attempts for that day, persist diagnostics, and keep heartbeat unhealthy through the session. Permanent auth/config/protocol failures retain the existing bot-run failure path. Fixed fallback symbols remain an explicitly configured existing option and are logged as fallback. No automatic fallback is inserted.
+
+## Verification and delivery
+
+TDD covers ratio/ATR/filter boundaries, completed-window coverage, holiday/DST, unknown instruments, finite numbers, auth separation, read-only endpoint paths, safe errors, Redis failure/locking/idempotence, job windows and read readiness. Command Center covers delayed readiness, retries/deadline, valid empty vs malformed, date/freshness and actual SIP paper signal/risk/fill/EOD exit. Platform focused tests, typecheck/build where available, cron/registry guards and Command Center full tests/harness run before delivery. Publish review branches/draft PR if supported; no merge or production deployment without approval. Native Windows installation remains a separate verified transfer step. Portfolio capital configuration remains pending and unchanged.
